Short:        MUI console for Amigas running amiagent
Uploader:     thomas@amiga-imager.com (Thomas Luebker)
Author:       thomas@amiga-imager.com (Thomas Luebker)
Type:         comm/net
Version:      0.4.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Distribution: Aminet
URL:          https://github.com/thomas-luebker/amifleet68
Requires:     MUI 3.8+, a TCP/IP stack, amiagent on the machines you watch

amifleet68 watches every Amiga on your network that runs amiagent, from
one MUI window on another Amiga. It is the Amiga-native sibling of
amifleet, the macOS console for the same fleet.

 - Fleet board: one row per machine, refreshed every five seconds -
   online state, round trip, agent version, CPU, OS, free Chip/Fast RAM.
 - Details: the full system report, an AmigaDOS shell (with Break for a
   command that hangs) and a file browser with Download and Upload.
 - Screen: the machine's front screen, grabbed through the agent. Works on
   any screen, even a Guru. Click, drag and type on the picture to drive
   that machine.
 - VNC: a client for AmiVNC. If AmiVNC is not running, amifleet68 starts
   it through the agent first. 256-colour "Fast" mode for 68k viewers.
 - Copy files: two panes, each on any machine - copy files and whole
   drawers between Amigas (or within one), Delete, Rename, MakeDir.
   Every path field has a drive popup with that machine's volumes,
   assigns and devices.
 - Scan network: finds every agent on your /24.
 - ARexx port AMIFLEET.1: MACHINES, STATE, POLL, ADD, DETAILS, SCREEN,
   VNC, COPYFILES, CONNECT, DISCONNECT.
 - AmigaGuide manual (Help key or Project/Manual).

Requirements
------------
 - AmigaOS 3.0+ (3.1 for planar drawing of remote screens), 68000 or
   better (amifleet68.020 for 68020+)
 - MUI 3.8+ (muimaster.library v19)          amipkg install mui38
 - bsdsocket.library: Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami
 - On each watched machine: amiagent 0.5.0+  (Aminet comm/net/amiagent)
 - Optional: AmiVNC for VNC                  (Aminet comm/tcp/AmiVNC.lha)

Installation
------------
Drag the amifleet68 drawer wherever you like and double-click the
program. The first run lists this machine's own agent; select it, click
Edit and enter your agent's TOKEN. Then Scan network, or Add machines.

Security
--------
amiagent runs any command for whoever knows its token, and the token and
all traffic are unencrypted. Keep the fleet on a network you trust.

Source (Apache 2.0) and issues: https://github.com/thomas-luebker/amifleet68
